Description:

A dissimilarity matrix shows the pairwise differences or distances between data objects.
It is a square, symmetric table with zero diagonal values.
Used in clustering, classification, and pattern recognition to find similarities and differences.
Different distance measures (e.g., Euclidean, Manhattan, Jaccard) are used based on data type.
In data warehousing, it helps in segmentation, pattern discovery, and anomaly detection.
